dex translator: drop constant readings nothing can load (last rescue)

A Dalvik constant is untyped, so each `const` is stored once per reading
TypeInference gives it: int AND float, long AND double. ConstReadingElision
drops such a store only when a later const of the same register overwrites it
in straight-line code outside every try range. That cannot touch a dispatcher:
each case sets its constant and jumps to a shared tail, and when the method is
`synchronized` the whole body sits inside the monitor's catch-all.

Translator.NEVER_READ_READINGS adds the global counterpart. Each (register,
reading) is its own JVM local, zeroed by the prologue and only ever given its
own scalar, so the store of reading S of register R can change behaviour only
for something that LOADS local (R, S). When no instruction of the method can --
no TypeInference use reads (R, S), no move copies R (emitMove copies every
reading), and no instruction outside the audited families names R -- that
store is dead at every const of R, whatever the control flow, handlers and
frames around it. Never ALL readings of a const, for ConstReadingElision's own
reason (a const that emits no code hands its label's frame to the next
instruction).

DexConverter arms it only after compact locals was not enough, as one more
step before the oversize stub, so every method that already converts -- the
one compact locals rescues included -- keeps its bytes.

Measured on Instagram 455 (228,034 classes): exactly one class changes,
X/0bRx (LauncherOverlayConfigLayer: the WebRTC overlay configuration read when
a call starts). getValues() is 11,265 instructions -- a loop over a dispatcher
of ~2,180 cases, 2,179 const-wide and 1,245 const, in a synchronized block:
    compact locals not enough for X/0bRx.getValues: 73744 -> 68914
    RESCUED X/0bRx.getValues()[I by compact locals + never-read constant
            readings: code_length 73744 -> 50891
Of its ldc2_w, 2,179 long remain and 0 double. The class links under
-Xverify:all, no STUBBED method is left in the jar, and boot is 3/3.

